# FoodMart | Sample E-Commerce Website

## About the Project

**FoodMart** is a sample e-commerce website developed as a learning and portfolio project using the Django web framework.

The main goal of this project is to practice web development concepts and learn how to transform a ready-made e-commerce HTML template into a dynamic website using Django.

In this project, selected parts of the FoodMart template have been customized and connected to the Django backend. Features such as product listing, shopping cart management, and dynamic data rendering have been implemented.

> **Note:** This project is an educational portfolio project and is still under development. It is not a complete production-ready e-commerce website. Features such as online payment and final order processing have not been implemented yet.

---

## Implemented Features

### Product Listing

- Displaying products stored in the database
- Retrieving product information through Django models
- Displaying product names, prices, descriptions, and images
- Showing products on the homepage
- Displaying available and active products

### Shopping Cart

- Adding products to the shopping cart
- Storing cart data using Django sessions
- Increasing and decreasing product quantities
- Removing products from the cart
- Calculating each product's subtotal based on its quantity
- Calculating the total cart price
- Displaying cart items and their information on the cart page

### Template Customization

- Using the FoodMart HTML template
- Customizing selected sections of the homepage
- Improving the display of product prices and stock quantities
- Removing duplicate quantity controls from product cards
- Customizing the Header and Footer sections
- Connecting shopping cart links to Django pages

---

